VALUES
  ('back-squat', 'leg-press', 'partial', 'injury_pain', 'Leg press still drives the hip, knee, and ankle flexion of a squat under load, so it keeps training the pattern when squatting causes pain.', 'mechanistic', 'strong', 12),
  ('back-squat', 'barbell-hack-squat', 'full', 'preference', 'Presented as a direct hypertrophy-focused stand-in for the back squat when someone can''t, won''t, or doesn''t need to test heavy squat strength.', 'experience', 'strong', 10),
  ('decline-barbell-bench-press', 'db-bench-press', 'partial', 'equipment', 'EMG studies show overall pec activity is similar between dumbbells and barbells, and dumbbells may even allow a deeper stretch at the bottom.', 'cited_study', 'strong', 6),
  ('assisted-pull-up-machine', 'lat-pulldown', 'full', 'skill', 'Both are vertical pulling movements that build the back comparably well, provided the load keeps progressively increasing over time.', 'experience', 'strong', 5),
  ('back-squat', 'front-squat', 'full', 'preference', 'Front squat and back squat are both squat-pattern lifts hitting largely the same muscles, unlike pairing overhead press with bench press.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 5),
  ('back-squat', 'leg-extension', 'partial', 'injury_pain', 'During a two-year injury layoff from squatting, isolation leg extensions kept building quad size without loading the spine axially.', 'experience', 'moderate', 4),
  ('back-squat', 'belt-squat', 'partial', 'injury_pain', 'Belt-squat-style machines load the hips and quads without routing force through the spine, sparing the back for deadlift work before a meet.', 'mechanistic', 'strong', 4),
  ('barbell-hack-squat', 'leg-press', 'full', 'preference', 'Both train quads through a similar movement pattern with long muscle lengths, full range of motion, and real overload potential.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 4),
