  ('dumbbell-lying-rear-lateral-raise', 'cable-lateral-raise', 'full', 'equipment', 'A single eight-week trial pitted the two moves against each other and found equivalent shoulder growth, despite each loading the muscle at a different length.', 'cited_study', 'strong', 4),
  ('reverse-grip-bent-over-row', 'chest-supported-row-machine', 'full', 'injury_pain', 'Chest support removes the lower-back loading of an unsupported bent-over row while still training the same pulling pattern, easing his back issues.', 'experience', 'strong', 4),
  ('seated-calf-raise', 'standing-calf-raise', 'partial', 'equipment', 'A cited study found the soleus, which seated raises target, responds poorly to training volume regardless of reps, so straight-knee standing work may cover it adequately.', 'cited_study', 'hedged', 4),
  ('seated-leg-curl', 'lying-leg-curl', 'inferior', 'equipment', 'Both flex the knee against resistance to load the hamstrings; lying leg curl is the standard fallback when no seated machine is available.', 'cited_study', 'strong', 4),
  ('barbell-curl', 'ez-bar-curl', 'full', 'injury_pain', 'An EZ-bar''s angled grip reduces the twisting force on the wrists and elbows compared to a straight bar, easing strain for less flexible joints.', 'mechanistic', 'strong', 3),
  ('barbell-squat', 'leg-press', 'inferior', 'injury_pain', 'The leg press supports the trunk and fixes the bar path, letting someone load the legs without the balance and spinal demands of a free squat.', 'experience', 'moderate', 3),
  ('bench-press', 'close-grip-barbell-bench-press', 'partial', 'preference', 'Both train the same maximal-force neuromuscular quality, so he treats moderate exercise swaps as acceptable, not just the exact competition lift.', 'mechanistic', 'hedged', 3),
  ('bench-press', 'incline-bench-press', 'partial', 'preference', 'Pressing at an upward angle shifted more relative muscle activity toward the upper pecs in most studies comparing incline to flat pressing.', 'cited_study', 'strong', 3),
