  ('back-squat', 'band-good-morning', 'partial', 'injury_pain', 'Good morning drills the torso-extension, hip-hinge portion of the squat pattern, complementing knee-extension work when you can''t load a full squat.', 'mechanistic', 'strong', 2),
  ('back-squat', 'smith-machine-hack-squat', 'full', 'preference', 'For lifters who stay upright, have no injuries, and good range of motion, these squat variations are essentially interchangeable for building muscle.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 2),
  ('back-squat', 'barbell-side-split-squat', 'partial', 'preference', 'Mentioned as another lower-fatigue option for a reduced-stimulus session, since single-leg work taxes the lifter less than a loaded bilateral squat.', 'mechanistic', 'hedged', 2),
  ('back-squat', 'sissy-squat', 'partial', 'preference', 'Sissy squats can hit the quads comparably well by MEV/RIR standards while spilling over into far less systemic fatigue than a loaded barbell squat.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 2),
  ('band-good-morning', 'rdl', 'full', 'skill', 'Both are barbell hip-hinge patterns for the posterior chain, but the RDL''s bar-against-the-legs path is simpler to learn and feels more stable.', 'experience', 'strong', 2),
  ('band-skull-crusher', 'reverse-grip-tricep-pushdown', 'partial', 'preference', 'Around 20+ reps the pecs and shoulders fatigue before the triceps on skull crushers, while pushdowns keep triceps as the limiter throughout.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 2),
  ('barbell-deadlift', 'trap-bar-deadlift', 'partial', 'preference', 'Both are heavy hip-hinge pulls from the floor, but the trap bar''s neutral grip keeps the torso more upright, shifting extra load onto the quads.', 'mechanistic', 'strong', 2),
