  ('reverse-grip-bent-over-row', 'db-row', 'full', 'injury_pain', 'In his example, barbell bent-over rows were straining someone''s lower back; dumbbell rows trained the same back muscles with no pain.', 'experience', 'strong', 2),
  ('reverse-grip-bent-over-row', 'barbell-row', 'full', 'injury_pain', 'Same example: machine rows also worked as a lower-back-friendly stand-in for barbell bent-over rows, training similar back musculature pain-free.', 'experience', 'strong', 2),
  ('reverse-grip-tricep-pushdown', 'band-skull-crusher', 'full', 'preference', 'Both isolate the triceps directly, so either works equally well to pre-fatigue the muscle before moving to dips.', 'experience', 'hedged', 2),
