  ('barbell-squat', 'db-squat', 'partial', 'equipment', 'Dumbbells can still train the quads without a barbell, but the load ceiling is much lower, so reps and proximity to failure must rise.', 'experience', 'strong', 1),
  ('barbell-squat', 'kneeling-cable-triceps-extension', 'inferior', 'injury_pain', 'When a lower-body injury rules out real squatting, isolating the quads on a knee-extension machine still lets you load the muscle.', 'experience', 'moderate', 1),
  ('barbell-squat', 'barbell-hack-squat', 'partial', 'preference', 'Hack squats let the legs reach genuine local failure in high-rep sets without the cardiovascular system cutting the set short first, unlike free squats.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 1),
  ('barbell-walking-lunge', 'smith-machine-lunge', 'partial', 'crowding', 'The fixed bar path lets you reproduce the same leg-drive stimulus in place, which matters when walking lunges would otherwise eat up the whole gym floor.', 'mechanistic', 'moderate', 1),
  ('barbell-walking-lunge', 'barbell-side-split-squat', 'partial', 'skill', 'A study found lifters new to training used much greater range of motion on split squats than lunges, since the fixed stance is easier to balance.', 'cited_study', 'strong', 1),
