  ('behind-the-neck-press-machine', 'ohp', 'full', 'injury_pain', 'Pressing in front avoids the extreme overhead-behind-head shoulder position that critics flagged as riskier for the joint.', 'experience', 'hedged', 1),
  ('bench-press', 'decline-barbell-bench-press', 'partial', 'preference', 'Pressing downward aligns better with the lower-pec fiber direction and lowered relative upper-pec and front-delt activity in some comparisons.', 'cited_study', 'hedged', 1),
